@page "/legal/ai"
<PageTitle>AI Disclaimer — CrowdFund AI</PageTitle>
<div class="page-container py-5" style="max-width:800px;">
    <h1 class="fw-bold">AI Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: 9 November 2026</p>
    <div class="cf-card">
        <p><strong>Trust scores, fraud flags, receipt extraction, and concierge answers are advisory.</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>They are risk indicators, not proof of legitimacy or fraud.</li>
            <li>They are not legal, tax, medical, or investment advice.</li>
            <li>Final publish, payout, and compliance decisions are made by humans and automated policy rules — not by the language model alone.</li>
            <li>Donation amounts, allocations, and ledger hashes are computed by deterministic server code, not by AI.</li>
            <li>Models can err, be incomplete, or be targeted by prompt injection; grounding and tool checks reduce but do not eliminate risk.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Donors should apply independent judgment. Creators must still comply with all applicable laws. See also <a href="/docs/limits">product limits</a> in the repository documentation.</p>
    </div>
</div>
